    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2bwllyra222",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The traffic from agent swarms doing research is going to be quite large, they are relentless at finding info. I had Fable 5.2 reconstruct WH Auden's 1941 poetry class. It found an obscure, relevant book on the Internet Archive, which it read a line at a time by doing repeated full text searches.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2bwllyra222",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-14T16:35:48.726Z",
      "likes": 88,
      "replies": 8,
      "reposts": 11,
      "score": 7.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 4.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n27qnrq3b222",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Got to see student presentations today at the Generative AI Studio at Penn. It was a visceral way to feel how far creative people can now get using AI. Already, almost every project from an individual was 10x further along than a fully done team project from three years ago.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n27qnrq3b222",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-13T19:44:19.916Z",
      "likes": 125,
      "replies": 11,
      "reposts": 8,
      "score": 6.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 25.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n27sqcs6ds22",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "\"You see the model called hydrogen is equivalent to the models called sonnet and luna and spark, but the model called fable is like wonder and astra and carbon (but it was like argon)\"\n\n\"Wait, why do you look confused?\"",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n27sqcs6ds22",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-13T20:21:32.404Z",
      "likes": 92,
      "replies": 7,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 6.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 24.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2762wfcot2x",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "The smaller scandal is that the White House has been perfectly happy to use export control laws against US AI companies like Anthropic while knowingly letting Nvidia get away with activities that arguably damaged national security.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2762wfcot2x",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-13T14:11:39.522Z",
      "likes": 14,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.3,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 30.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2762wfcos2x",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "The larger issue is that Nvidia was selling to Megaspeed in Singapore, which is known to be smuggling chips to China. The White House and Trump knew about it and were not enforcing export controls while simultaneously talking about  the AI arms race against China.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2762wfcos2x",
